WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
Every facility has a way
its day is supposed to run.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.700
Breakfast has a time.
Rooms have responsibilities.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.880
Equipment needs checking. And people
need to be in the right places.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.860
But how does the software know
how your facility operates?

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.620
With Vssyl, it starts in Build.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.360
First, you establish your facility.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.900
Its floors, neighborhoods, kitchens,
serving areas, and equipment.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.300
Then, you add the departments you need

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.900
and define how each operates
within those spaces.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.020
Set your operating rhythm.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.380
Breakfast begins at seven-thirty.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.760
Serving stations need to be ready
beforehand.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.200
Define the staffing coverage
each location requires.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.120
Establish the records your team needs
to complete, and when they're expected.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.280
Review your configuration,
and publish it when you're ready.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.100
That's Build.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.220
The operating plan behind your facility.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.580
But creating the plan
is only part of the story.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:57.460
Now, it's time to put that plan
into action.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.440
Welcome to Run.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.640
The same facility you just configured

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.800
becomes a visual, interactive view
of your daily operations.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.240
For supervisors and managers,
the Dashboard brings together

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.800
what's happening now, what needs
attention, and what's coming next.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.260
Open a location, and you'll find
the equipment that belongs there,

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.520
who's assigned to work there,
and the current state of its operation.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.560
Open Employees, and you can see
who's scheduled, who's working,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.780
and where they've been assigned.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:27.120
And as the day progresses,
records are completed,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.940
service milestones are confirmed,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.600
and the operational picture changes
to reflect what's actually happening.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.020
Run isn't another setup screen.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.160
It's your operation, in motion.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.440
And when you need to change
how your facility operates tomorrow?

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:41.920
You return to Build.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.840
Make your adjustments, review them,
and choose when they'll take effect.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.980
Without rewriting what happened today.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.440
Build defines the expectation.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.660
Run captures the reality.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:56.160
Together, they connect the way
your facility is designed to operate

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.680
with the people who keep it moving.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.540
Vssyl.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.380
Build the plan. Run the day.
